lesson k-rolling-down-a-ramp v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=7 subject=physics levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Rolling down a ramp"
  goal "Say that a steeper slope sends a ball faster and further, count how far it rolls, and say why a rough floor stops it sooner."

  look {
    scene 30x14 {
      ramp r1 height=5 ball=0 rolled=10 at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
      A ball let go at the top of a slope rolls down and keeps going along the floor. The higher
      and steeper the slope, the faster it goes and the further it rolls. A rough floor like a
      carpet slows it down sooner.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.steeper-faster k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.steeper-faster count=2 seed=2
    practice k.how-far-rolled count=2 seed=3
    practice k.ramp-further count=2 seed=4 easy-count=1
    practice k.bigger-push count=1 seed=6
    practice k.push-or-pull-job count=1 seed=7
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.rough-floor
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.knock-the-cup a=6 b=3 easy-a=7 easy-b=2 hard-a=5 hard-b=3
  }
  remember {
    say "Steeper goes faster and further. Rough floors slow things down."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud. A plank on a pile of books and a toy car are the whole lesson: add a
    book and roll again, and let the child say what changed. Change only the height each time, so
    the test is fair. If the child is stuck, remember the park slide. Off the page, roll a ball on
    the kitchen floor and on a rug from the same slope. Japan, 幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten
    guidelines), 環境, 内容 (7): "身近な物や遊具に興味をもってかかわり，考えたり，試したりして工夫して遊ぶ。"
    (Take an interest in familiar things and toys, and play inventively by thinking and trying
    things out.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the steep slope is chosen in the teacher's pen first, the rolls are short, and the balls to compare stop far apart."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the questions turn round to ask for a slow roll, the rolls are long, and the balls and cups to compare are close."
  }
}
